declareVariable -- assigns an input gate to a given variable name
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        declareVariable x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, or an *note IndexedVariable:
        (Macaulay2Doc)IndexedVariable,
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note InputGate: Gate,, 

Description
===========

This method assigns an *note InputGate: Gate, which has the same *note Name:
(Macaulay2Doc)newPackage, as the given symbol or the *note baseName:
(Macaulay2Doc)baseName, of the given *note IndexedVariable:
(Macaulay2Doc)IndexedVariable,, so that later references to the symbol will be
treated (and can be used) as an *note InputGate: Gate,. This can be reverted
with *note undeclareVariable: undeclareVariable,.

+----------------------+
|i1 : declareVariable x|
|                      |
|o1 = x                |
|                      |
|o1 : InputGate        |
+----------------------+
|i2 : x + 1            |
|                      |
|o2 = (x + 1)          |
|                      |
|o2 : SumGate          |
+----------------------+

See also
========

  * *note undeclareVariable: undeclareVariable, -- clears assignment of an
    input gate to a variable name

Ways to use declareVariable:
============================

  * "declareVariable(IndexedVariable)"
  * "declareVariable(InputGate)"
  * "declareVariable(Symbol)"
  * "declareVariable(Thing)"

