evaluating gates
****************

The standard method *note value: (Macaulay2Doc)value, provides a way to
evaluate *note Gate: Gate,s at particular inputs, provided in the form of a
*note ValueHashTable: valueHashTable,. The results are cached, and thus are not
recomputed when called again with the same *note Gate: Gate, and *note
ValueHashTable: valueHashTable, as inputs.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : declareVariable X                               |
|                                                     |
|o1 = X                                               |
|                                                     |
|o1 : InputGate                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : declareVariable Y                               |
|                                                     |
|o2 = Y                                               |
|                                                     |
|o2 : InputGate                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = sumGate {X+Y,Y,X}                           |
|                                                     |
|o3 = ((X + Y) + Y + X)                               |
|                                                     |
|o3 : SumGate                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : D = productGate {X*Y,Y,C}                       |
|                                                     |
|o4 = ((X * Y) * Y * ((X + Y) + Y + X))               |
|                                                     |
|o4 : ProductGate                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : h = valueHashTable({X,Y},{1,ii})                |
|                                                     |
|o5 = ValueHashTable{...2...}                         |
|                                                     |
|o5 : ValueHashTable                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : v = value(D,h)                                  |
|                                                     |
|o6 = -2-2*ii                                         |
|                                                     |
|o6 : CC (of precision 53)                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : v == product{value(X*Y,h),value(Y,h),value(C,h)}|
|                                                     |
|o7 = true                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note valueHashTable: valueHashTable, -- creates a hash table of values for
    evaluation
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

